window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: System, Let's Unbind Ourselves","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi had died.","Then she came back to life.","But how long she could stay alive—hours, days—was still unknown.","“Pain... it hurts so much!!!”","The moment Jiang Yunxi regained even a sliver of consciousness, she was engulfed by endless agony.","They said pain came in thirteen levels. Jiang Yunxi felt that what she was experiencing had to be level fourteen.","The emperor of all emperors.","It was like a massive truck was running over her body again and again.","A fragment of her memories from before she lost consciousness resurfaced.","“So death is this painful.”","She had thought it was a final burst of awareness before death and had quietly waited for her consciousness to fade away. Yet instead, her mind grew clearer and clearer.","“What’s going on? Wasn’t I already dead? Then how...”","“Has Miss woken up yet?”","“Not yet.”","Two unfamiliar voices reached her ears, and Jiang Yunxi froze.","What was this “Miss” business?","Didn’t they call people in hell things like this ghost or that ghost?","Did ghosts need to sleep too?","The next instant, those questions seemed to trigger some kind of switch. Her head throbbed, and a flood of memories came rushing in.","Just as she was about to sort through them, an excited voice rang out in her mind.","【Host, you’re finally awake!】","【Host, I’m your System Sprite.】","Caught completely off guard by the voice, Jiang Yunxi nearly had a heart attack.","She could practically see her great-grandmother waving at her.","【Host, aren’t you surprised? Delighted?】","【I checked your memories. I know you’ve always wanted a storage space and a system!】","A System Sprite... and it was hers!","She had bonded with a system. Did that mean she wasn’t dead after all?","After reading novels for so many years, Jiang Yunxi had seen people bond with systems before—but never ghosts.","What was more, although she had not yet had time to organize the memories that had just flooded into her mind, she had caught glimpses of them.","Those memories did not belong to her.","Memories that weren’t hers, plus a system... as a veteran web-novel reader, Jiang Yunxi arrived at one conclusion.","She had transmigrated.","【System, what exactly is going on?】","【How did you bind to me?】","【Am I still alive?】","System: 【Host, you died, but then you came back to life.】","Jiang Yunxi: The art of saying nothing had truly been mastered by this thing.","Her body hurt too badly for her to waste time bantering with the system, so she impatiently urged, 【Speak plainly.】","System: 【I am speaking plainly.】","Sensing the intense fluctuations in its host’s emotions, the system did not dare keep joking and hurriedly explained.","【When you thought that, since you already had terminal cancer and only had a few days left to live anyway, you might as well trade your life for someone else’s and chose to take a bullet for a Chinese soldier, you died.】","【Completely and utterly dead.】","Jiang Yunxi: 【Then how did I come back to life?】","【Did you save me?】","The System Sprite spoke rapidly.","【To be precise, it was the Chinese soldiers who saved you.】","【It was my first time carrying out a mission. Because I was inexperienced, I went to the wrong time and space and happened to pass over your world.】","The System Sprite’s tone was full of chagrin.","【Those soldiers were desperate to save you after you were critically injured protecting their comrade. Their urgency was so strong, and their magnetic field so intense, that it affected me.","Somehow, I ended up binding with you after your body died and your soul left it.】","【The Main System discovered that I had gone to the wrong time and space—and even bound myself to the wrong host—so it came to correct the mistake.】","Yet, bound by the merit of those soldiers, the military souls and accumulated merit of the entire Huaxia armed forces were protecting you. It couldn’t forcibly sever the bond.","If it accidentally caused your soul to scatter and vanish, the System Realm would have thoroughly offended Huaxia.】","You Huaxia people are not easy to provoke. Setting aside the ancient great powers, even the hosts bound to various systems over the years would form a considerable force if they joined together.","【The Main System had no choice but to make the best of a mistake and kick both your soul and me, your system, into this time and space.】","【The Main System said that hosts can be replaced, but the time and space cannot.】","The Main System had even secretly instructed it to keep a close eye on her and make sure she didn’t get herself killed.","With all that merit and the protection of Huaxia’s military souls, if anything happened to her...","Forget this little shrimp of a system—even the Main System wouldn’t get away unscathed.","Naturally, the system didn’t dare let its host know that. It was afraid she would become reckless, knowing she had nothing to fear.","And then...","Jiang Yunxi understood.","She was glad that, in that moment, she had followed her instincts.","She had traded what little life she had left for the soldiers’ safety, never expecting such an outcome.","She had been given another chance at life, and she even had a system by her side.","She believed that, back in the modern era, the country would not treat her family unfairly.","The money they had borrowed for her treatment should be enough to pay off, and there might even be some left for her parents.","Although she had an older sister, so her parents would not be left without anyone to care for them in their old age, this at least proved that she had not been entirely useless.","This deal, Jiang Yunxi felt, was an absolute steal.","From what the system had just said, she had also picked up some information: apparently, she had powerful backing.","Even the Main System did not dare offend it, much less this little system.","Perhaps, from now on, when she did things...","Fortunately, the system could not access every thought in her mind. Otherwise...","【Why does everything hurt so much?】","【You brought me into this body—did you harm its original owner?】","【If you did harm her, who would be responsible for that?】","With merit protecting her body and all this transmigration business, Jiang Yunxi was beginning to believe in such mystical matters.","If she had harmed the original owner of this body because of her arrival, would that karma fall on the system—or on her?","Surely it could not be her fault. She had not asked the system to place her in this body.","If anyone was to blame, it should be the system—or the Main System!","【Rest assured, Host. Before you entered this body, its original owner had already died.】","【This system is a law-abiding, upstanding system. I would never do something as cruel as taking a life without regard.】","Jiang Yunxi did not feel even the slightest bit embarrassed.","Such matters had to be made clear from the start, otherwise there would be disputes later on.","【Then how did the original owner die?】","【It wasn’t revenge, was it? Am I safe now?】","【My whole body hurts. Is it because the original owner was injured, or because my soul and this body are incompatible and rejecting each other?】","【Can my soul remain in this body?】","【And what kind of system are you?】","【Please don’t tell me you’re some kind of mission system or romance-conquest system.","Let me tell you, I hate doing missions most of all, and I hate having to pursue and win over someone even more.","I’ve been single since birth. I’ve never dated, I don’t know how to date, and I definitely don’t know how to win someone over.】","【If failing missions or being unable to conquer the target means I’ll be erased, then you might as well let me die right now.】","[So I won’t have to spend every day on edge afterward, worrying that one day I might fail to complete a mission...】","Relying on what she believed was her backing, Jiang Yunxi made her stance clear right away: she didn’t want to do missions, and she didn’t want to pursue or win over anyone.","Jiang Yunxi fired off so many questions in a row that she completely stunned the system.","Hadn’t she wanted a system very badly? Why was she being so picky the moment they bonded?","Hosts these days were far too difficult to manage. She was the worst host it had ever had.","The system was deeply relieved that, before the Main System had kicked it over here, it had worried that the host might fail her missions and die, thereby offending Huaxia. So it had modified the system core.","Otherwise...","The system’s silence made Jiang Yunxi’s heart skip a beat. Could the system she’d bonded with really be a mission system—or some kind of romance-conquest system?","Then she was doomed.","She might as well give up immediately.","Having read plenty of novels, she knew those two kinds of systems were complete traps. If you failed a mission or didn’t reach the required affection level, they’d shock you with electricity or strike you with lightning.","Someone like her would be finished sooner or later.","If she was going to die sooner or later anyway, she might as well die sooner and reincarnate sooner.","Maybe, with all that accumulated merit, she could be reborn in Huaxia. Eighteen years later, she’d be a fine young woman again.","【System, let’s unbind.】"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: System, I Have It So Hard","paragraphs":["【System, let’s sever our bond!】","The words struck like a thunderbolt out of nowhere, crashing the System’s CPU.","The System never imagined that merely failing to respond in time would earn it a threat from its Host to sever their connection.","It hadn’t even done anything! It had only been thinking about how to answer its Host.","After all, it had originally been designed as a mission system. But then the Main System made a change, giving it the functions of two different systems.","The Main System had instructed it to let its Host enjoy gossip without risk or worry, while also finding a way to have the Host complete the original system missions without her knowing.","If a mission wasn’t completed, the punishment originally meant for the Host would instead fall on it.","Although the severity of the punishment had been reduced somewhat, it would be delayed until after this Host severed their bond, when it would be reflected in the System’s overall KPI evaluation.","When the person who was originally supposed to be punished was the Host, but the punishment had instead become its responsibility, even the System Sprite felt that it was getting a raw deal.","It felt there was nowhere it could go to seek justice.","But the Main System had said that if it hadn’t run into the wrong time-space and accidentally become bound to its current Host while gossiping, none of these troublesome matters would have happened afterward.","If it didn’t take the blame, then who would?","Even so... despite that... it still felt wronged.","It had taken such a huge risk for its Host, and not only did the Host know nothing about it, she was even threatening to sever their bond.","As a novice system binding itself to a Host for the first time, if its Host voluntarily severed the connection right after the binding, the only thing awaiting it would be being sent back for reconstruction.","Its system life was supposed to have begun with it making a name for itself in the world of systems. Instead, it was about to end before it had even started.","It kept its Host in its heart, while its Host kicked it straight into a ditch.","The System was suffering.","The System was crying pitifully.","It hurriedly sought help from the Main System, asking whether it could conceal its identity as a mission system, lest...","It was having such a hard time.","Had the Main System forgotten that it was only a novice system too? Could it really shoulder such a huge responsibility?","You’re afraid of Huaxia and don’t dare let my Host die, so you come bully me instead.","Fortunately, because of Jiang Yunxi’s special nature, the Main System had been paying close attention to the situation on their side. Its reply arrived in an instant.","After receiving the Main System’s response, the System hurriedly answered,","【Host, rest assured. This System is neither a mission system nor a strategy system. It’s merely an ordinary Gossip System.】","Jiang Yunxi felt inexplicably disdainful of the Gossip System. What use was there in binding herself to a gossip system?","Gossip was only good for passing the time!","With that time, she might as well play on her phone or read novels.","Come to think of it, where had she been transported? Were there phones and tablets here?","Jiang Yunxi had received far too many memories, and her entire body was in unbearable pain. She had no mind to sort through them just then, so she simply asked directly,","【System, you still haven’t told me what era this is, or what happened to the original owner of this body.】","【Ding—】","【The Gossip System is now officially at your service.","As for the gossip concerning this body—in other words, you, Host—would you like to hear it?】","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Yunxi: 【Tell me.】","How could she refuse? At the very least, this would help her figure out her current identity—and let her see whether this Gossip System was actually any good.","The System inhaled sharply: I’m very good.","The System: 【The original owner of this body was also named Jiang Yunxi.】","Jiang Yunxi: “Good. At least I won’t have to get used to another name.”","[She is currently nine years old, the Fifth Miss of the Marquis of Pingyang’s household, a daughter born to Madam Zheng, the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang’s Secondary Wife.","Because she was born after a difficult labor that left her in poor health, she had always been kept deep within the inner chambers and rarely went out.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······”","From “the Marquis of Pingyang’s household,” “daughter of a secondary wife,” and “the Heir’s Secondary Wife,” she deduced that she had transmigrated to ancient times.","Wasn’t the modern era perfectly fine? If not that, she could at least have gone to some interstellar future. Why did it have to be ancient times?","Please, let it not be the dynasty with the queue hairstyle.","Jiang Yunxi immediately interrupted the System. [System, don’t tell me I’ve transmigrated into the Qing dynasty, okay?]","[Rest assured, Host. This is not the Qing dynasty. It is a dynasty that does not exist in your history—the Yunzhao Kingdom.]","So it was an entirely fictional world.","Fictional was good. Fictional was wonderful. Fictional was absolutely fantastic.","A fictional world meant that no matter what she did here, she would not alter the history of her own timeline.","With the huge weight in her heart finally lifted, Jiang Yunxi urged, [Go on.]","[Yesterday was a holiday from the household academy. The original host was playing hide-and-seek with the maids in her family’s rear garden.","She hid behind a particular ornamental rock, never imagining that someone would sneak up behind her, knock her unconscious with a stick, and quietly throw her into the lake.]","[By the time she was rescued, she had been soaking in the water for far too long and remained unconscious.","The blow to her head had caused a blood clot in her brain. On top of that, she had been submerged for so long that her lungs became infected. With her high fever refusing to break, she eventually died.]","Jiang Yunxi frowned. [So this is an inner-household power struggle?]","What kind of inner-household power struggle was this? It was even more brutal than palace intrigue. They were using real weapons and actually killing people.","At this rate, how many people could possibly be left alive in the Marquis of Pingyang’s household?","The fact that the entire household had not already been wiped out was probably a miracle.","Jiang Yunxi asked with complete confidence,","[Was the person who did it acting on the orders of the original host’s primary wife? Or was it one of her legitimate or secondary sisters? Or perhaps one of the other concubines of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang?]","As if she hadn’t read countless novels all these years.","Aside from those people, who else would want to get rid of the original host?","Sigh. Why had she transmigrated to ancient times? And why had she ended up as a physically frail daughter of a secondary wife?","Jiang Yunxi was deeply worried about her future.","With enemies lurking everywhere, could she, a complete novice at inner-household intrigue, survive in the marquis’s household with the help of this seemingly unreliable Gossip System?","Just listen to her title: the Fifth Miss.","In ancient times, sons and daughters were generally ranked separately. From that title alone, it was obvious that the Marquis of Pingyang’s household had quite a few children.","The struggle for power was sure to be······","[Host, you’re mistaken.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······” Why did her face feel so hot?","She had only just tried to show off her cleverness, and she had already been proven wrong.","Was there a crack in the ground she could crawl into?","Or perhaps someone could bring her a block of tofu so she could bash her head against it.","Pretending nothing had happened, she said, [You say I’m wrong, so why don’t you tell me who actually knocked out the original host and threw her into the water?]","[They must have been trying to drown her, right?]","The System replied, [It is true that someone wanted to drown her, but it wasn’t any of the people you just listed.]","[The original host could only be called unlucky. She chose the wrong place to hide while playing hide-and-seek with the maids.","There was a cave not far from the ornamental rock where she was hiding. Two people were inside playing cards.]","[The original host made a noise, startling the two of them.","They saw the original host and thought she had discovered them. To keep their secret from getting out, they decided to silence her for good.]","Jiang Yunxi was baffled. [Playing poker is just playing poker. Why would they kill someone just because they were seen?","It was only a game of poker! Was that really worth it?]","Was it worth taking the original host’s life?","As soon as the words left her mouth, Jiang Yunxi froze. She suddenly recalled the movie recaps she used to watch on TikTok.","Aside from card games, “playing poker” seemed to have another meaning.","It was all the System Sprite’s fault for being so up-to-date—she hadn’t caught on right away.","Suppressing the urge to cough awkwardly in her mind, Jiang Yunxi quickly cut off the System before it could explain.","[All right, no need to explain. I know what “playing poker” means now.]","[Just tell me who that shameless pair is.]","Now that she had taken over this body, the original host’s enemies were her enemies. She had to avenge her.","Just then, the voice of a middle-aged woman drifted over.","“Has Fifth Miss woken up yet?”","“The Old Madam has been worrying about her. She sent me over to take a look.”","The System’s voice suddenly turned shrill. [Host, it’s her.]"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: She's here, she's coming with rat poison","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi was in the middle of asking the system who had killed the original owner when a woman’s voice suddenly rang out.","At the same time, the system shrieked, 【Host, it’s her.】","Her? What did it mean, “her”?","Oh. It was talking about the pair of adulterers who had killed the original owner.","But did it mean the woman who had spoken, or the Old Madam she had mentioned?","The Old Madam... Jiang Yunxi drew in a sharp breath. Wasn’t that the original owner’s grandmother?","The woman who had committed adultery and killed the original owner couldn’t be the Old Madam—the original owner’s own grandmother, could it?","If it really was the Old Madam, how was she supposed to avenge the original owner?","Destroying her own clan outright?","Would she be struck by lightning for that?","Just as Jiang Yunxi was growing increasingly uneasy, the system spoke again.","【The nanny who just spoke is the woman from that adulterous pair. Her name is Nanny Kong, an old servant from your grandmother’s quarters.","As for the man, he’s her lover—the steward in charge of the stables in the outer residence.】","Good. There was no need to worry anymore. It wasn’t the Old Madam.","【Steward Ma was the one who knocked the original owner unconscious with a club. Nanny Kong then threw her into the lake.】","Excellent. She had found the culprits. Nanny Kong and Steward Ma, was it? Just wait until this young lady recovered. She would make sure the two of them paid with their lives for the original owner’s death.","The system spoke again.","【Host, there’s some juicy gossip about Nanny Kong. Do you want to hear it?】","Of course she did. This was the perfect opportunity to learn more about her enemy.","【Spill!】","【Nanny Kong was a young maid whom the Old Madam brought over from her maiden family. Later, the Old Madam arranged her marriage to a servant of the Pingyang Marquis’s Residence.","Her husband made a mistake once and was expelled from the residence.","Because Nanny Kong had pleaded with the Old Madam on his behalf, she escaped being implicated and continued serving at the Old Madam’s side.】","【Since the man had been dismissed for committing an offense, he had a blemish on his record and could never find a decent job. He survived by relying on Nanny Kong to support him.","But he was the sort of man who enjoyed living off a woman while still acting like her master. Whenever he was in a bad mood, he took it out on Nanny Kong. After suffering this way for years, the couple gradually grew estranged.】","Did Jiang Yunxi feel sorry for Nanny Sun?","At first, a little. But the moment she remembered that this woman had killed the original owner, all her sympathy vanished.","Instead, she felt that Nanny Kong deserved everything coming to her. Sometimes, only a villain could deal with another villain.","【Nanny Kong’s life was miserable, and Steward Ma happened to be acquainted with her husband. Knowing about her circumstances, he took advantage of her vulnerability and comforted her repeatedly. The two of them eventually began an affair.","And once they started, it continued for many years.】","【Oh, and Nanny Kong’s second son is actually Steward Ma’s child.","Fortunately, the boy resembles Nanny Kong, so no one else noticed anything.】","Impressive. Jiang Yunxi almost wanted to applaud them.","They had carried on an affair in a crowded and watchful marquis’s residence for so many years. They had even produced a child, yet no one had discovered them.","The original owner had really been unlucky. She hadn’t even uncovered their affair. Just because they suspected her, she had been...","【Host, this is bad!】","Jiang Yunxi’s heart jolted.","【Nanny Kong has come with murderous intent. The handkerchief hidden on her contains rat poison.】","【She’s afraid you’ll wake up and expose her affair with Steward Ma. She’s here to finish the job and silence you for good!】","Damn it! This woman was ruthless. She had actually come back to deliver a second blow!","What was wrong with people in ancient times? Did human life really mean so little to them?","Jiang Yunxi tried to call for help, only to discover that this body seemed to be beyond her control. She couldn’t even open her eyes, let alone get up and cry for help.","Sensing her struggle, the system hurriedly explained:","【Host, this body currently has pneumonia and a high fever. On top of that, your soul has only just entered it and hasn’t adapted yet, so you won’t be able to wake up for a while.】","Jiang Yunxi panicked.","【Then what do we do? Hurry up and save me!","I’m lying here completely helpless. Isn’t that just making it convenient for her to poison me?】","【You and I are in the same boat now. If one of us prospers, we both prosper; if one of us suffers, we both suffer. You can’t just stand by and watch me die.】","Although she had threatened the system earlier, saying that if it made her complete missions and pursue men, she would rather die sooner, Jiang Yunxi still didn’t want to die now that the moment had actually arrived.","After all, a bad life was still better than no life.","And besides, she would be dying at the hands of her enemy.","If she let her enemy have her way, she was afraid she wouldn’t be able to rest in peace—even the lid of her coffin might not stay shut.","【Host, I can’t do anything right now.","I can only speak inside your mind. It’s not as if I can call for help on your behalf.】","Jiang Yunxi was furious. What a useless system! She had known it couldn’t be relied on.","With such a worthless system, how was she supposed to survive in this ancient world, where she had been thrown straight into a life-or-death crisis?","【System, after I die, I’m going to file a complaint. I’ll report your entire system realm for treating human lives as worthless.","You only know how to bind yourselves to hosts. You don’t take responsibility for anything else. You’re all about killing without bothering to bury the dead.】","The system’s CPU nearly began smoking.","What should it do? Its host was about to die, and it was unlikely to complete the main system’s mission.","The system realm was certain to offend Huaxia, and it would inevitably be sent back for reprogramming as well.","The system glanced over its administrative interface. It was so familiar, yet so strange. It had to memorize every detail. After this, it might never see them again.","Suddenly, it spotted two lines of data, and its eyes lit up.","【Ding! Host successfully consumed the original owner’s gossip. Gossip Points +300.】","【Ding! Host successfully consumed Nanny Kong’s gossip. Gossip Points +100.】","Jiang Yunxi, who was preoccupied with saving her own life, barely paid attention when she heard the two notifications.","【Host, there’s a way!","I have a system shop. You can use 100 Gossip Points to unlock it, then buy an Antidote to All Poisons.","That way, even if she poisons you, you won’t have to worry.】","At that moment, the system’s voice sounded like the most beautiful, wonderful music in the world to Jiang Yunxi.","【Unlock it, unlock it! Do it now!】","【Buy it, buy it! Get it immediately!】","【All right, Host. I’ll unlock the system shop and purchase the Antidote to All Poisons right away.】","It felt as though a century had passed. In reality, less than five seconds later, the system spoke hesitantly.","【Host, the purchase failed. You don’t have enough Gossip Points.】","What a useless system!","Had it been deceiving her just now?","Didn’t it know the prices of the items in its own shop?","【How many points are we short?","Can’t you give me a discount, or let me buy it on credit?】","【Discounts and credit both require approval from the main system.】","More procedures. Always more procedures. At that moment, Jiang Yunxi hated those procedures with every fiber of her being.","【Then hurry up and get approval.】","Although she was speaking only in her mind, Jiang Yunxi felt as if she had shouted herself hoarse.","While Jiang Yunxi and the system were discussing Nanny Kong’s secrets and desperately trying to find a way to save her life, Nanny Kong had already finished speaking with the maids and matrons in Jiang Yunxi’s courtyard. She was now walking step by step toward Jiang Yunxi, who lay on the bed.","Nanny Kong’s footsteps were steady. Each step landed on the gray brick floor with a soft click-click, like someone striking Jiang Yunxi’s heart with a hammer and making her nerves draw taut.","To her ears, that sound was no different from the approach of the Grim Reaper.","She was coming. She was coming, carrying rat poison with her.","At that moment, Jiang Yunxi’s soul, which was already poorly attuned to the body, seemed ready to leave it again.","She struggled desperately to open her eyes and call for help, but her body felt as though it had been nailed to the bed. She couldn’t move a muscle, and not even the faintest sound could escape her throat.","All she could do was listen as the footsteps drew closer and closer, becoming clearer with every step, until they finally stopped beside her bed.","“Poor Fifth Miss!”","Jiang Yunxi felt someone gently stroking her face. The touch was incredibly light, yet to her it felt as heavy as a thousand jun.","That ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍voice belonged to Nanny Kong.","Clearly, it was Nanny Kong who was touching her.","Was the next step going to be pressing a handkerchief smeared with rat poison over her face...?","“How could you have fallen into the lake so carelessly and nearly drowned yourself like this?”","“Nanny, just hearing about it makes my heart feel as though it’s being torn apart. I can only imagine how the Old Madam must feel.”","Jiang Yunxi thought, “Aaahhh... That Kong woman, you poisonous old hag! Stop putting on such a shameless act. Wasn’t it you and your lover who attacked me from behind, knocked me unconscious, and threw me into the lake, leaving me in this state?”","Outside the room, a woman staggered on her feet and nearly fell."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Zheng, what did I hear","paragraphs":["The woman was none other than Madam Zheng, the biological mother of the original owner, Jiang Yunxi, and the Secondary Madam of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang. She glanced around, but there was no one there.","Then what had been the voice she heard just now...?","“Suju, did you hear anything?”","Suju shook her head. “Madam, this servant didn’t hear anything.”","Madam Zheng was astonished. “You didn’t hear it? You didn’t hear a woman’s voice?”","Suju shook her head again. “This servant truly didn’t hear anything.”","Madam Zheng frowned. The voice continued to ring in her ears.","【That vile Nanny Kong, that old hag! If you wanted to have an affair with Steward Ma, couldn’t you do it in your own home? Why did you have to sneak around in the Marquis’s Residence?","I caught you in the act, and because you were afraid I’d expose you, you decided to kill me.】","【How dare you two commit regicide!】","【You’ve already harmed me so badly that I’m unconscious, yet you still won’t let me go.","You actually came back to silence me a second time, and now you’re trying to poison me with rat poison.】","【If I really die, I’ll haunt you even as a ghost!】","【Is anyone there? Hurry and send someone! Save this poor child!】","【Heavens above, earth below, open your eyes! Strike this murderous pair of adulterous dogs dead!】","【My dear father and mother, come save your daughter!","I don’t want to be killed by my enemies a second time!】","【This lousy System is useless too! It said it would think of a way to save me, then vanished without a trace!】","【I don’t want to die twice in one day!】","Madam Zheng’s expression changed drastically. Even if she had been a fool, she would have understood who the owner of that voice was by now.","It was her Yunxi.","Although she didn’t understand why the maid couldn’t hear it while she alone could, this was not the time to worry about that.","Someone was trying to poison her Yunxi with rat poison.","Madam Zheng lifted her skirts and hurried forward in great strides.","Suju was stunned. What was wrong with the Secondary Madam? Why had she completely abandoned all concern for propriety?","It seemed that Fifth Miss had been running a high fever and remained unconscious for so long that even the Secondary Madam had lost her composure.","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍Yunxi felt the hand on her face withdraw.","“Why is Fifth Miss sweating so much?”","Another voice rang out, clearly belonging to a young woman.","“Nanny Kong, the Young Miss has had a high fever that won’t go down. She’s been breaking out in cold sweats constantly.”","“Then let this old servant wipe her sweat for her.”","The moment she heard that, Jiang Yunxi was terrified out of her wits.","【Ahhh! Nanny Kong, that poisonous old hag, is going to wipe my face with a handkerchief contaminated with rat poison.","If she rubs it over my nose or mouth, won’t I be doomed to remain unconscious forever?!】","【Someone help! Save me! Murder!】","【System, Main System, I hope your nineteenth-generation ancestors are doing well! I’m throwing in one extra generation—no need to thank me.】","Although she couldn’t open her eyes and see anything, Jiang Yunxi seemed to have developed a third eye. She could almost picture a fierce-looking old nanny with a face full of flesh and a vicious expression, wearing a benevolent smile as she held a handkerchief.","【Young Miss, Nanny loves you!】","【Love my head!】","【You wretched Nanny Kong, send my regards to your second—】","The door was suddenly shoved open with a tremendous bang. It rebounded, only to be held open by someone.","At the same time, a woman’s furious shout rang out.","“Stop! Stay away from my daughter!”","Hurried footsteps sounded. Jiang Yunxi heard someone rush over, shove Nanny Kong away from the bedside, and pull her into her arms.","Her face was abruptly buried in a soft bosom. That softness...","At that moment, Madam Zheng’s heart was pounding violently, as though it might leap straight out of her mouth.","The nanny standing beside her daughter just now had been Nanny Kong, the Old Madam’s personal attendant. She had even been holding a handkerchief and was about to press it against her daughter’s face.","She must be the “vile Nanny Kong” and “old hag” mentioned in that voice. And that handkerchief...","That voice had truly been Yunxi’s.","Nanny Kong had been shoved back several steps without warning. She only managed to steady herself by grabbing the bedpost.","She frowned as she looked at Madam Zheng, who was holding Fifth Miss.","Although Madam Zheng was the Secondary Madam of the Heir, Nanny Kong was a trusted servant of the Old Madam and had never considered the Heir’s concubine worthy of her attention.","She gave a cold laugh. “Madam Zheng certainly has quite the imposing manner.”","“This old servant came out of the goodness of her heart to visit Fifth Miss on behalf of the Old Madam and help wipe her sweat, yet you nearly injured me.”","“Are you dissatisfied with the Old Madam, Madam Zheng? Are you planning to defy her?”","“You’re talking nonsense! I have no dissatisfaction with the Old Madam. It’s clearly you...”","Madam Zheng opened her mouth, wanting to repeat what Jiang Yunxi had said, but the moment she tried to mention it, no sound came out.","“Yunxi said...”","She tried several more times and finally understood. She could hear her daughter’s strange inner voice, but she was apparently forbidden from telling anyone else about it.","Just then, the voice rang out again.","【This is my mother? My real mother?","Mother, could you not hold me so tightly? You’re a little too well-endowed—I’m practically suffocating.】","【Don’t let Nanny Kong and her lover drown me, and don’t let the rat poison kill me, only for me to end up suffocating in your arms.】","Madam Zheng was now one hundred percent certain that what she was hearing was indeed her daughter’s inner voice.","She quickly loosened her hold on the girl, but didn’t dare let go completely.","She was afraid that Nanny Kong might use the handkerchief in her hand...","The handkerchief! Right—the handkerchief!","Her daughter’s inner voice couldn’t be revealed to others, so she couldn’t use it to bring down Nanny Kong and her lover. But wasn’t the handkerchief in Nanny Kong’s hand proof enough?","“Quick, come and seize Nanny Kong! Take the handkerchief from her!”","“Have someone examine it carefully and find out exactly what’s on it!”","The maids and older servants in the room froze.","Nanny Kong, however, was startled. How did Madam Zheng know there was something wrong with the handkerchief?","Feeling guilty, she tried to stuff it into her sleeve while saying, “Madam Zheng, what do you mean?”","“This old servant came to see Fifth Miss out of the goodness of her heart, yet you’ve ordered people to seize me and inspect the handkerchief in my possession?”","“Could it be that you suspect this old servant harbors ill intentions toward Fifth Miss?”","Nanny Kong’s stern voice and obvious guilty reaction immediately aroused suspicion in the maids and servants, who had initially thought Madam Zheng’s order was rash.","They no longer hesitated and immediately followed Madam Zheng’s instructions, surrounding Nanny Kong.","Nanny Kong naturally tried to escape. The rat poison on the handkerchief could not be explained away.","But even with all her strength, she was no match for so many people. She was quickly subdued.","“Madam Zheng, you’d better remember that I belong to the Old Madam. You dare—”","“Enough,” Madam Zheng interrupted her. “Tie Nanny Kong up and gag her. Isn’t the physician waiting in the room next door? Go and bring him here. Have him examine the handkerchief carefully.”","【Host, I’m back.】","【Host, the Main System agreed. From now on, you can borrow against your account. The limit is only one thousand, though.】","Just like in those Hong Kong movies—the police always showed up at the very last moment.","【System, why didn’t you wait until I was dead before coming back?】","【If I’d relied on you, the grass on my grave would already be three feet tall.】","【As expected of a useless System. When it really mattered, I still had to rely on my mother.】","Still, how did my mother know there was something wrong with Nanny Kong’s handkerchief?","Could it be that she caught Nanny Kong tampering with rat poison?","The System quickly scanned the situation and soon figured out what had happened while it was searching for the Main System.","Once it understood everything, it felt rather embarrassed. It was all the Main System’s fault—why had it gone off to deal with the aftermath in another time and space at a moment like this? It had caused quite a delay.","Fortunately, the host’s biological mother had rescued her. Otherwise...","To make amends, the System scanned Nanny Kong once more and uncovered even more of her secrets.","【Host, when Nanny Kong and her lover were harming you, they were seen by a craftsman who had come to repair the railing around the lake. He was the one who told people that you had fallen into the lake.","He’s currently debating whether to use this to blackmail...】"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: System, Where's My Compensation","paragraphs":["The System was just preparing to atone for its mistakes by telling Jiang Yunxi that it had found witnesses who could establish the guilt of those two when Madam Zheng’s personal maid hurried in.","“Madam, this is bad! The physician just said that the handkerchief Nanny Kong used to wipe the young lady’s face contained a large amount of rat poison.","“Nanny Kong was trying to harm the young lady.","“The physician would like to come in and examine her thoroughly.”","Madam Zheng felt a little annoyed that the maid had come in at such an inopportune moment, interrupting her daughter’s conversation with that so-called System.","Still, she had heard the most important part: the craftsmen who had repaired the railing by the lake on the day her daughter fell into the water. Now she knew who they were.","“I understand. Go and invite the physician in.”","Thinking of Nanny Kong’s attempt to harm her daughter, Madam Zheng knew she had to inform the Heir and Madam as well.","Although she was a secondary wife, that title was merely a pleasant one. In the end, she was still a concubine and had no authority to deal with such a matter.","“Send someone to invite the Heir and Madam too, and tell them that Nanny Kong tried to harm the young lady.”","“And also...”","Her daughter might be unconscious, but her mind was clearly awake.","Madam Zheng did not want them to know that she could hear her daughter’s thoughts.","“We’ll discuss it outside.”","Madam Zheng carefully laid down the daughter she had been holding close in her arms, then left the room with Suju.","Jiang Yunxi: [Useless System, did you hear that? Nanny Kong was caught red-handed. The rat poison in the handkerchief is evidence. We don’t need you at all.]","[You really are completely useless. When I needed you to save my life, you were nowhere to be found. Now that someone else has saved me, you’ve come crawling out to take credit.]","[From now on, all I need is my mother. She can keep me alive. All you do is send me to my death!]","The System blocked both its host and the Main System, then continued cursing up a storm. Its language was truly foul.","It was just unclear whether it was cursing its host, the Main System, or both.","When she still received no response from the System after a long while, Jiang Yunxi frowned.","[System, why aren’t you saying anything? Do you think I’m right?]","The System’s voice came through, sounding somewhat ingratiating.","[Host, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍you can’t blame me this time. It was all the Main System’s fault. It wasn’t here just now...]","[Enough with the excuses. I nearly died because of you two. Don’t you think I deserve compensation?]","[Compensation?] The System raised its volume, dragging out the final syllable. [But you’re fine, aren’t you?]","Jiang Yunxi arched a brow.","[The fact that I’m fine is thanks to you?]","The System hurriedly contacted the Main System. Fortunately, the Main System did not drop the ball this time.","[Compensation is possible.]","The corners of Jiang Yunxi’s lips curled upward.","That was right—she had earned four hundred Gossip Points from gossiping twice earlier. She had spent one hundred to unlock the System Shop, leaving her with three hundred.","But three hundred points were not enough to exchange for a Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill...","Jiang Yunxi cleared her throat.","[System, tell me about this Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill. How many points does it cost?]","[The Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill is exactly what its name suggests. After taking it, one becomes immune to all poisons. It can prevent any poison found in the mortal world.","[There are three versions. The low-grade version costs five hundred Gossip Points and lasts for five years. The mid-grade version costs seven hundred Gossip Points and lasts for ten years. The high-grade version costs fifteen hundred Gossip Points and lasts for life.]","She had transmigrated to ancient times, and she was a concubine-born daughter. There was probably no avoiding the struggles of an inner household.","Poisoning was one of the most common methods used in such schemes, and it was extremely difficult to guard against.","She really needed this Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.","And if she was going to get one, she wanted the best.","[System, I’m a very easily satisfied person. I’m not greedy at all.","[For my compensation, I’ll take the high-grade Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.]","[It’s only fifteen hundred points. That’s just a few pieces of gossip. It’s not much at all, don’t you think, System?]","[Beeep...]","An emotionless electronic voice rang out.","[Warning. The System has insulted its host. One warning issued.]","Jiang Yunxi arched a brow.","[System, you dare insult me? I think my compensation is too low now. That System Shop of yours...]","[Agreed, agreed. The compensation will be the high-grade Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.] The System’s voice was filled with urgency.","It was worried that if it hesitated any longer, its host would raise the price again.","It would have to speak seriously with the Main System later. This host was far too crafty. The Main System needed to grant it greater authority, otherwise next time—","[Hand it over!]","System: [Host, you can’t move your body right now. Even if I give it to you, you...]","[It should dissolve the moment it enters my mouth, right? After all, it’s made by the System?] Jiang Yunxi asked.","That was how it always worked in the novels she had read.","The System sounded rather proud.","[Of course.]","Jiang Yunxi relaxed.","[Then put it directly into my mouth.]","Good things had to be safely secured—or rather, safely swallowed.","What good was it to leave it in someone else’s hands? What if the System pocketed it or switched it with something else?","Jiang Yunxi deliberately left the System unblocked so that it could hear her private doubts.","Soon, she felt a foreign object suddenly appear in her mouth. A sweet, refreshing flavor spread through her, followed by a warm current that rose throughout her body and lingered for quite some time.","[Host, this body was weak from birth because of a difficult delivery. You’ve been taking medicinal decoctions for years, and there’s quite a lot of medicinal toxicity accumulated in your body.","[After taking the Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill, those accumulated toxins have been cleansed as well. Your body should feel somewhat lighter and more comfortable.]","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes lit up, and she hurriedly asked:","[What about my inherent weakness?]","The System’s answer immediately shattered her hopes.","[Host, it’s a Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill. It’s for detoxification and poison prevention, not for treating illness.]","Jiang Yunxi clicked her tongue. Fine. There went her hopes.","Then perhaps the System Shop had something else...","[Does the System Shop have any medicine for treating physical weakness?","[I can’t drag around this sickly body forever. How am I supposed to go out and gather gossip to earn Gossip Points?]","Although the System had no heart and therefore could not experience a pounding one, it felt as if its CPU were about to crash again.","This crafty host—what was she planning now?","Surely she wasn’t about to demand more compensation!","[Host, let me make one thing clear first. You’ve already received your compensation, and you’ve already used it. You have to keep your word. You can’t go back on it.]","[So there is something?] Jiang Yunxi asked, not entirely certain.","[There is, but you’ll have to earn it through gossip. You can exchange Gossip Points for it later. It won’t be free.]","Jiang Yunxi felt that the System was looking down on her. Had she ever said she wanted it to give her something for free?","Could it not question her character?","Although... well, she had not actually said that part out loud.","[How many pills would I need to completely cure this body, and how many Gossip Points would they cost?]","[One Health-Strengthening Pill is enough. It’s not expensive—five hundred Gossip Points.]","Only five hundred. That really was not expensive. She already had three hundred, so she only needed to gather gossip a few more times.","There was no hurry to deal with her physical weakness. She had plenty of time in the future. Her priority now was staying alive.","She had to remember that she currently had a cerebral hematoma, pneumonia, and a high fever that would not go down. If nothing was done, she would end up just like the original host.","But she only had three hundred Gossip Points. Would that be enough to deal with all these illnesses?","She also had to save those points to cure her physical weakness.","The System had sent her into this body. Didn’t that mean it bore some responsibility?","Still, judging from the System’s reaction just now, it clearly had no intention of offering any additional compensation.","She’d still have to rely on it to make money from gossip in the future, so she couldn’t push them too hard. She needed to come up with another plan—see if she could fleece them for a little more and squeeze out some extra benefits.","Once this opportunity passed, it might never come again.","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes flickered as she said nonchalantly,","【System, we’re already bound together. You owe me the newbie gift pack, right?】"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Newbie Gift Pack, It Can Be Available","paragraphs":["Seeing that there was no way to keep exploiting the compensation loophole and fleece the System, Jiang Yunxi could only find another way.","Her eyes turned, and she said, 【System, according to the rules of your system world, every host gets a beginner’s gift package after binding with a system.","Where’s my beginner’s gift package?】","The System was dumbfounded. Hosts received beginner’s gift packages after binding with a system? Why had it never heard of that?","It certainly had not been mentioned during its pre-job training.","Nor was there any such provision in its rules.","The System said, 【Host, are you sure you’re not mistaken? I’ve never heard of any beginner’s gift package.】","【How could there not be one? Every host bound to a system gets a beginner’s gift package.】","Jiang Yunxi was completely unreasonable, yet utterly confident. After all, she had backing.","This was her only chance to fleece the System, so how could she let it pass?","【System, don’t forget that this body is still unconscious. I have a high fever and pneumonia, and apparently there’s even a blood clot in my brain.","I might kick the bucket at any moment.】","【Are you sure the medicine in this era can cure me?】","If it could, the original owner would not have died from this illness.","【High fever and pneumonia—either one of those could be fatal in ancient times.","This body was already weak to begin with. If the fever keeps burning, how many hours do you think I can last?】","【What if I accidentally kick the bucket? Huaxia...】","Jiang Yunxi stopped there, making her point without saying too much.","Since the Main System had been so worried about her dying earlier, it should still be concerned now.","She ought to be able to use that concern to force some good things out of it.","【Putting everything else aside, you have to give me medicine to dissolve the blood clot in my brain, bring down the fever, and cure the pneumonia.","This was the original owner’s mess, after all. You can’t expect me to waste my gossip points treating it.】","At that thought, Jiang Yunxi suddenly realized that the Body-Strengthening Pill should probably be paid for by the System too. After all...","Having received the thoughts in Jiang Yunxi’s mind—and seeing the response the Main System had just sent it—the System hurriedly cut in before she could speak again.","【The beginner’s gift package, right? Yes, yes, we have one.】","The Main System had just replied that, from now on, as long as Jiang Yunxi’s requests cost no more than one thousand gossip points, the System no longer needed to ask for approval and could make its own decisions.","The Main System was worried that if it failed to respond in time again, it would be forced to pay compensation, or that Jiang Yunxi might actually die and then Huaxia...","However, the Main System had also said that it could not satisfy her every demand. Even when it did, it had to keep the price as low as possible and minimize its losses.","Medicine to clear the blood clot, reduce the fever, and treat pneumonia were all very ordinary medications. They were barely worth anything.","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes lit up. She had fleeced the System again.","But the System had agreed far too readily this time. There had to be a catch.","No, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍she had to ask for more.","【You need to prepare plenty of these medicines for me, in case the treatment doesn’t work.","Especially fever reducers. You need to prepare lots of those.","There’s no air-conditioning in this era, and winters are so cold that it’s easy to catch a cold or come down with a fever. With this frail body of mine, I could easily kick the bucket.】","The System gritted its teeth.","【Fine, no problem. I’ll put enough cold medicine in your beginner’s gift package for you to take every day for three months.】","It was being awfully generous. Apparently, cold medicine cost practically nothing in the System’s world.","Then...","【How can three months possibly be enough? This body is so weak...】","【Six months. I’ll give you enough to take every day for six months. Not one day more.】","Jiang Yunxi was delighted, though inwardly she put on a coy expression and asked, 【What about the expiration date?】","【Ten years. I’ll give you medicine with a ten-year shelf life. I guarantee it won’t go to waste.】","【Fine, then.】 Jiang Yunxi sounded indifferent. 【Give me some side-effect-free painkillers too. My whole body hurts.】","【All right.】","The System’s voice sounded somewhat listless.","There was nowhere for Jiang Yunxi to store all these things at the moment, so they could only be placed in the System’s inventory. She still felt uneasy about that.","It was like owning something without actually having control over it.","The main problem was that the System was far too unreliable.","She wondered whether the System Shop sold things like spatial rings. If it did, perhaps...","But then she thought of how the System had looked just now.","Forget it. She should not push it too far. She would still have to rely on it to earn gossip points in the future.","She had to take a long-term approach.","Still, she was a little unwilling to let the matter go.","【A beginner’s gift package definitely ought to include bonus gossip points.","Other people’s beginner’s gift packages all come with points rewards. I should get some too.】","【All right, no problem.】","Without giving Jiang Yunxi another chance to make a request, a mechanical voice rang out.","【Host, please claim your beginner’s gift package.","Would the host like to claim it?】","That was a ridiculous question. Naturally, she answered, 【Claim it.】","【Would the host like to open the beginner’s gift package?】","【Once opened, all items in the gift package will automatically be stored in the System’s inventory.】","【Open it, open it!】 Jiang Yunxi said impatiently.","【Beginner’s gift package opened. You have obtained: five Blood-Clot-Dissolving Pills, three full courses of pneumonia medication, eighteen boxes of fever reducers, ten boxes of ibuprofen, ten bottles of hemostatic powder, three bottles of diarrhea pills, five boxes of anti-inflammatory medicine, five bottles of cough syrup, five bottles of iodine solution, and 300 gossip points.】","Excellent. She was quite satisfied with this gift package.","Jiang Yunxi eagerly summoned the System interface. Her gossip-point balance was now 600, and she could also see the items in the System’s inventory.","【The Body-Strengthening Pill only costs 500 points, and I can exchange for it now. Should I...】","Forget it. She would wait until later.","That thing took effect immediately after being swallowed. The medical attendant was keeping watch over her right now. If she took it and suddenly recovered, wouldn’t she be exposed?","【System, give me some fever-reducing and pneumonia medicine first.","And don’t forget the medicine to dissolve the blood clot.】","Not long after taking the medicine, perhaps because of its effects, Jiang Yunxi began to feel drowsy. Somehow, she drifted off to sleep.","When it sensed that its host had fallen asleep, the System finally let out a sigh of relief.","That little schemer had finally gone to sleep.","In the past, when it had chatted with its seniors in the system world, they had all said that their hosts were very obedient and treated them like divine beings, fawning over them as if they were their grandfathers.","Why was its own host completely different? The host was the grand master, while the System was not even as important as a grandson.","And it was not the only one inferior to a grandson. Even the Main System...","Was Huaxia really so impressive just because it had soldiers and a military spirit? Even the Main System was afraid of it!","No, it had to take advantage of the host’s sleep and hurry to ask its senior systems what exactly was going on with Huaxia.","Clearly, Huaxia was not someone—or something—to offend.","...","After Jiang Yunxi fell asleep, Madam Zheng followed a middle-aged couple into her bedroom.","Upon seeing the three of them, the maids and older women keeping watch in the room hurriedly bowed and greeted them.","“Your Highness, the Heir’s Wife, Madam.”","Madam Zheng had been on edge the entire way, afraid that her daughter would keep muttering her thoughts and the two of them would hear everything.","Although she had already confirmed that no one besides herself could hear them, what if the Heir and the Heir’s Wife could?","Her daughter’s inner voice was completely different from the quiet, introverted way she had behaved in the past. Madam Zheng was worried that Jiang Yunxi would be reprimanded. Even more, she feared that they might take away her right to raise her.","Fortunately, the entire walk to the door had passed in silence, and only then did she finally relax.","She glanced at her daughter, who lay motionless on the bed. She did not know why Jiang Yunxi had clearly regained consciousness but still had not woken up.","Nor did she know why she herself could hear her daughter’s inner voice.","But Madam Zheng did not feel the slightest bit afraid anymore. Instead, she felt deeply fortunate.","She was fortunate that she had been able to hear her daughter’s inner thoughts and rescue her in time. Otherwise, her daughter might have been killed by that adulterous pair, while Madam Zheng herself would have ended up feeling grateful to Nanny Kong for coming to visit her daughter.","She had no idea what the System that allowed her to communicate with her daughter actually was, or whether it could awaken her.","From what the two of them had said, her daughter seemed to be short of money—so short that she had to buy things on credit.","How could that be acceptable? Although her daughter was only a concubine-born daughter, she was still a young lady of the marquis’s household. How could she ever be made to worry about money?","It seemed that Madam Zheng had been wrong to think her daughter was still young and never went out, and therefore not give her much spending money. She had allowed others to look down on her daughter.","Madam Zheng glanced at the Heir ahead of her.","Her daughter had suffered so much, and the chief culprit was none other than the Old Madam’s trusted nanny. Surely the Heir couldn’t remain completely indifferent.","Perhaps she needed to have a serious talk with him."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Young Master, the concubine is ill.","paragraphs":["Looking at the pale-faced Jiang Yunxi lying on the bed, her principal mother, Madam Liu, said with a pained expression,","“Fifth Girl has truly suffered this time.","“It’s all the fault of that vile pair. If it weren’t for them, Fifth Girl would never have ended up in such a state.”","According to the household physician, Fifth Girl’s condition was extremely critical. She had always been frail, and after nearly drowning, she developed inflammation in her lungs. Her high fever refused to break, and there was a good chance she might not survive.","Though the child had not been born from her womb, Madam Liu had watched her grow up.","It had been Madam Liu who had arranged for Madam Zheng to enter the household back then. Although Madam Zheng was useless and had been brought in to suppress Madam Wei, she had ultimately failed to do so.","Fortunately, Madam Zheng had always treated Madam Liu with respect over the years, and the two children she had borne had likewise been respectful toward her.","Keeping the mother and son in the household helped showcase Madam Liu’s virtue, so naturally, she did not wish for Jiang Yunxi to meet with disaster.","After all, Jiang Yunxi was merely a concubine-born daughter. When the time came, Madam Liu could simply send her out with a dowry, and she would pose no threat to Madam Liu’s own children.","Although the girl was still young, she was already remarkably beautiful. If she could marry into a good family, she might even be able to support her eldest brother in the future.","With that thought in mind, Madam Liu naturally had no objection to currying favor with Madam Zheng.","“Heir, Nanny Kong and Steward Ma plotted against Fifth Girl. We have both witnesses and physical evidence,” Madam Liu said solemnly.","“They dared to commit such filthy acts in the residence and even plotted to harm their young mistress. Even if they were cut to pieces, it would not be excessive.”","“You must not let them off simply because Nanny Kong serves in the Old Madam’s quarters and was one of the Old Madam’s dowry maids.”","Madam Liu knew that, given Madam Zheng’s position, it would be inappropriate for her to say such things.","If word got out, Madam Zheng would inevitably be criticized for disrespecting her mother-in-law and overstepping her authority.","Madam Zheng could not say it, but as the lady in charge of the household, Madam Liu certainly could.","Moreover, Madam Liu was genuinely furious—and frightened.","In broad daylight, those two had dared to commit such an indecent act in the rear garden, engaging in an illicit affair.","If word spread, people would say that the Marquis’s household had terrible morals, and the marriage prospects of the children in the residence would suffer as a result.","This time, Fifth Girl had encountered them. But if it happened again and the victim was Eldest Daughter, then the one they silenced would be her Fei’er.","The moment Madam Liu imagined that the motionless girl on the bed was her Fei’er, a chill ran down her back.","She became even more determined that, even if the Old Madam objected, she would make the Heir and the Marquis report those two to the authorities and have them severely punished.","After hearing the Heir’s Wife, Madam Zheng also looked at the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang, Jiang Fengtang, with anticipation.","Naturally, she wanted those two dealt with as well.","They had attempted to kill her daughter several times. If they were let off lightly, wouldn’t everyone assume that she and her children were easy targets and continue bullying them in the future?","Looking at his daughter lying unconscious on the bed, Jiang Fengtang was likewise filled with fury.","He had few children—only four sons and three daughters—and treasured every one of them. Naturally, he did not want anything to happen to any of them.","This youngest daughter in particular had been frail since childhood. It had taken great effort to raise her to this age, and she had nearly lost her life at the hands of servants.","The household physician had even said that he could not be certain whether she would wake up, and had urged Jiang Fengtang to find an imperial physician to examine her.","Thinking of the adulterous pair who had caused all this, Jiang Fengtang hated them to the core.","He said coldly, “Let them off? How could that be? I’ll have their lives.”","“In a moment, I’ll have them bound and brought before Father and Mother. I’ll tell them everything and send them to the authorities for punishment.”","“They dared to murder their mistress. Not only will they pay, their families won’t escape punishment either!”","Madam Liu and Madam Zheng were naturally very pleased with the Heir’s answer.","Madam Zheng was just about to thank the Heir and the Heir’s Wife when a commotion arose in the courtyard, drawing everyone’s attention.","Madam Liu frowned. “What are the servants in the courtyard doing? Don’t they know that Fifth Girl needs quiet to recuperate? How can they be making such a racket?”","She turned to Madam Zheng. “Madam Zheng, Fifth Girl is still young, and the servants in her courtyard likely don’t obey her properly.","“When you have time, you should help her discipline those servants. Don’t let them take advantage of their young and inexperienced mistress to bully her.”","“If a maid or senior servant had been accompanying her this time, that vile pair would never have succeeded.”","Madam Zheng did not think the Heir’s Wife was using the opportunity to criticize her before the Heir or imply that she was an uncaring mother who had failed in her duty to guide her daughter. Instead, she fully agreed.","“The Madam is right. I have indeed been neglectful,” she said. “From now on, I will properly discipline the servants in Yunxi’s courtyard and guide Yunxi as well.”","Hearing the commotion outside, Jiang Fengtang’s anger also surged. He said sternly to Madam Zheng, “If anyone refuses to submit to your discipline, go to the Madam—and come to me as well.","“We will stand up for you.”","Madam Zheng hurriedly curtsied. “Then I thank the Madam and the Heir in advance.”","At that moment, someone outside began shouting loudly,","“Heir, the concubine is feeling unwell and wishes you to go see her.”","“Heir, the concubine is ill and wants Physician Wu to examine her.","“But ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍Fifth Miss’s people have kept the household physician here and refuse to let him go. Fifth Miss and Madam Zheng clearly don’t regard the concubine at all. Please go and uphold justice for her!”","Hearing the somewhat familiar voice, everyone in the room knew who had arrived.","It was Chunlan, the senior maid serving Madam Wei.","The maids serving the Heir’s Wife had always been given names beginning with “Xia,” meaning summer. Madam Wei, wishing to outshine the Heir’s Wife, had given most of the maids around her names beginning with “Chun,” meaning spring.","Madam Liu could not help sneering. “Madam Wei is ill again?","“Of the three hundred and sixty-five days in a year, is there a single one when she isn’t sick?","“Even Fifth Girl, who was born after a difficult delivery and has always been frail, and Younger Sister Zheng, whose health was damaged, have not been ill as often as she has.”","“She merely wants to win favor through illness. After all these years, does she think no one can see through her?”","Jiang Fengtang’s face darkened.","Although that might have been true... his wife did not need to put it so bluntly.","“She simply heard that I sent someone to summon you home early and assumed something important had happened. She was afraid the benefits might fall into someone else’s hands, so she wanted to intercept you, charm you into submission, and keep the advantage for herself.”","Jiang Fengtang’s expression darkened further.","“And now she claims that there’s no household physician available because Madam Zheng and Fifth Girl are withholding him?","“She’s so well-informed—could she really not know that Fifth Girl has been unconscious for two days and still hasn’t woken up?”","“Madam Zheng has been keeping watch over Fifth Girl for two days as well. When would she have had the time to scheme against Madam Wei?”","Madam Zheng was also seething with anger. For once, she disregarded her usual restrained nature and her habit of avoiding competition with Madam Wei. She curtsied and said,","“Heir, I did not stop anyone from taking the household physician.","“I have been here with you and the Madam, questioning those two people just now. I had no idea that Younger Sister Wei had sent someone to ask for a physician.”","“Besides, there is more than one household physician in the residence. The one staying here with Fifth Girl is Physician Chen, who has always been responsible for tending to the health of the young masters and misses and specializes in pediatrics. He is not Physician Wu, whom Madam Wei usually uses.”","Jiang Fengtang suppressed his anger and said, “I know. This is not your fault.”","Even if the residence had only possessed one physician and Madam Zheng had truly withheld him, Jiang Fengtang would still have thought it was justified.","No matter how much he favored Madam Wei ordinarily, when his daughter’s life was at stake, he was not foolish enough to lose his judgment.","Chunlan continued shouting outside, completely ignoring the servants’ reprimands. Looking at his daughter lying quietly on the bed, Jiang Fengtang was overcome by an extraordinary fury.","He strode out of the room and into the courtyard, where he bellowed furiously,","“Have you no sense of propriety at all?","“You’re nothing but an ignorant servant, yet you dare run into the young miss’s courtyard and make such a scene. You’ve shown complete disrespect toward the Secondary Madam and the young miss. Is this how Madam Wei taught you?”","“My lord, the concubine is ill—”","“She’s ill every other day. Do you really think I don’t know that not a single one of those illnesses is genuine?” Jiang Fengtang cut her off.","The servant had clearly been spoiled by Madam Wei. Instead of admitting her wrongdoing when reprimanded, she actually dared to argue back.","Thinking of his own daughter, who had been harmed by two servants who knew nothing of their place, and seeing the resentment on the maid’s face, Jiang Fengtang took his anger out on her.","“Since Madam Wei doesn’t know how to teach her servants, I’ll teach her myself.”","“Someone gag her and bind her outside the courtyard. Give her thirty strokes of the cane.","“When you’re finished, throw her back to Madam Wei and have her teach her properly.","“If there’s a next time, sell her outright.”","“And punish Madam Wei by making her copy the household rules twenty times.”","...","When Madam Wei saw Chunlan being carried back like a torn rag and heard the messenger repeat the Heir’s words, her hand slipped. In a fit of rage, she accidentally knocked over the tea set, vases, and other furnishings in the room.","“Madam Zheng, Jiang Yunxi, just you wait!”"]}]);
